mhvtl for Debian
================

Differences from the default build
----------------------------------

Media is stored in /var/lib/mhvtl, the FHS location for variable state data
(Debian Policy 9.1.1 reserves /opt for software the distribution does not
ship). This matches the upstream default.

The kernel module is not built during the package build. mhvtl-dkms ships the
source and DKMS builds it for the running kernel. Kernel headers matching that
kernel must be installed, otherwise the build fails and no module is
installed.

Starting the service
--------------------

A systemd generator creates one daemon instance per entry in
/etc/mhvtl/device.conf, so the units are templates and are not enabled
individually. After editing the configuration:

    systemctl start mhvtl.target

If /var/lib/mhvtl is empty, run make_vtl_media(1) once to create the media.

Why the daemons run as root
---------------------------

vtltape and vtllibrary create their own character device node with mknod() in
chrdev_create(). The kernel module registers a dynamic character major but
never calls device_create(), so no uevent is emitted and udev cannot create
the node instead.

CAP_MKNOD alone is not sufficient. mknod() also needs write permission on
/dev, which is root-owned and mode 0755, so the call fails with EACCES before
the capability is consulted. CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE lifts that restriction but
grants root-equivalent file access.

Running unprivileged is possible: mknod() on an existing path returns EEXIST,
which chrdev_create() treats as success. It requires a privileged step to
create and chown the nodes before the daemons start. That belongs in the
shared systemd units rather than in the packaging, so it is not done here.

The units drop the privileges that are not needed: NoNewPrivileges, a
CapabilityBoundingSet of CAP_MKNOD, CAP_SYS_RESOURCE and CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE, and
the ProtectSystem, ProtectHome, ProtectKernel* and Restrict* directives.
PrivateDevices stays off because it would replace /dev with a private instance
and hide the mhvtl nodes.
